            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're running a trucking business, every dollar matters. And when it comes to expanding or replacing your fleet, one of the biggest questions is whether to buy new or used.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "On paper, a used truck might look like the more affordable option, but once you factor in semi truck maintenance costs, it could be better to buy new.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we work with Florida's truck owners every day to help them make smart, long-term decisions. Let's break down what really goes into the cost of ownership, and how a new semi truck can actually save you money in the long run.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-used-tradeoff",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding the Maintenance Trade-Off with Used Trucks",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "used-tradeoff"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-used-tradeoff-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "There's no doubt that used trucks can be a smart solution for many owner-operators, especially when purchased from a trusted dealer with a strong inspection and service process. However, older trucks naturally come with more miles and more wear on major components. Over time, that can lead to more frequent repairs, from brakes and transmissions to electrical systems. These aren't always deal-breakers, but they do require budgeting and planning.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-used-tradeoff-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the biggest challenges is the risk of downtime. Every hour a truck is off the road is time that isn't generating revenue, and depending on the size of your operation, that can quickly impact schedules and customer satisfaction. For some, those extra maintenance windows are manageable. But for others, especially businesses without backup units or extra capacity, even a couple of unexpected breakdowns a year can disrupt operations and margins.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-new",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why New Semi Trucks Could Be a Smarter Investment",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-new"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-new-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "New trucks are built for performance and reliability. With a factory-fresh engine, brand-new components, and no history of wear, maintenance costs are significantly lower in the first few years. Here's what you can expect:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-new-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Fewer roadside breakdowns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Longer intervals between services"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lower cost of ownership over time"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-new-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Plus, many of the new International® models available at Sun State International include factory warranties that cover key repairs, giving you peace of mind while protecting your investment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-why-new-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-why-new-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
